IMPORT prelude

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore) -- who needs a licence and what unlicensed broadcasting costs (ss 8, 46, Second Schedule);
-- satellite dishes (ss 20, 47, First Schedule); supporting proscribed foreign services (s 30); unauthorised decoders (ss 48, 48A);
-- control of broadcasting companies (ss 32, 33, 35, 36, 41); foreign funding and foreign ownership (ss 43, 44); and the
-- egregious-content offences for online services and internet access providers (ss 45D to 45J).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BA1994.txt, with amendments
-- to S 738/2024 (in force 25 September 2024) shown. The deposit annotates s 8(5), (6) "[Act 4 of 2008 wef 01/04/2024]", which is
-- reproduced as found.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 17 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a broadcaster, an investor,
-- a shopkeeper, an online platform or an internet access provider actually meets. Not encoded: Ministerial directions (s 3), Codes
-- of Practice and licence modification, suspension and cancellation (ss 6, 10 to 13), public service and must-carry obligations
-- (ss 14 to 19), frequency planning and broadcasting conditions (ss 22 to 28), declared foreign services (s 31), Ministerial
-- approval criteria and directions (ss 37, 39, 40, 42), the regulated online communication service regime (ss 45K to 45O), powers
-- of investigation (ss 50 to 52), and the transitional provisions. "Substantial shareholder" is defined by reference to s 81 of
-- the Companies Act 1967, which was not read: it is taken here as a fact supplied by the user.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Broadcasting Act 1994 -- licensing and control`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the smaller of` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `8, 46 and Second Schedule -- licensable broadcasting services`

-- s 8(1): "A person must not provide any licensable broadcasting service in or from Singapore without a broadcasting licence"
-- granted under s 8 or a class licence under s 9.
-- Second Schedule: 20 items, among them free-to-air and subscription television and radio (nationwide, localised, international),
-- special interest services, audiotext, videotext, teletext, "Video-on-demand services", broadcast data services and "Computer
-- online services". But "a delivery system is not to be deemed to be a licensable broadcasting service by reason only that
-- facilities or expertise are provided for the delivery of any broadcasting service".
-- s 46: fine up to $200,000 or 3 years or both, and for a continuing offence a further $10,000 "for every day or part of a day"
-- after conviction.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `free-to-air nationwide television`
    `subscription nationwide television`
    `free-to-air localised radio`
    `a special interest television service`
    `a video-on-demand service`
    `a computer online service`
    `a teletext service`
    `a delivery system that only provides facilities`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is licensable` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `a delivery system that only provides facilities` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service, `provided in or from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a broadcasting or class licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `providing the service is an offence under s 46` IF
    `the service is licensable` `the service` AND `provided in or from Singapore` AND (NOT `holds a broadcasting or class licence`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed broadcasting` MEANS
    200000 PLUS 10000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `20, 47 and First Schedule -- satellite dishes`

-- s 20(1): a person must not (a) install broadcasting apparatus, (b) import, offer for sale, sell or possess it for sale, or (c)
-- operate or have it on premises owned or occupied by the person, "except under and in accordance with a licence".
-- First Schedule: the only broadcasting apparatus is a "Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)", meaning
-- apparatus "(including a dish antenna) ... capable of direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing through
-- any communication or broadcast satellite".
-- s 20(3): no licence is needed by a person working the apparatus "in the course of the person's duty as a member of the Singapore
-- Armed Forces, the Singapore Police Force, the Vigilante Corps or the Singapore Civil Defence Force". (4): the Authority may exempt.
-- s 47: fine up to $40,000 or 3 years or both, and the apparatus "shall be forfeited".
DECLARE Apparatus IS ONE OF
    `a satellite dish receiving broadcasts directly`
    `a terrestrial television aerial`
    `a television set`

DECLARE Operator IS ONE OF
    `a private householder`
    `a shopkeeper`
    `a soldier on duty`
    `a police officer on duty`
    `a Vigilante Corps member on duty`
    `a civil defence officer on duty`
    `a private security guard on duty`

GIVEN `the apparatus` IS A Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the apparatus is broadcasting apparatus` IF
    CONSIDER `the apparatus`
    WHEN `a satellite dish receiving broadcasts directly` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the operator` IS A Operator
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator is exempt by s 20(3)` IF
    CONSIDER `the operator`
    WHEN `a soldier on duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a police officer on duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a Vigilante Corps member on duty` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a civil defence officer on duty` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the apparatus` IS A Apparatus, `the operator` IS A Operator, `holds an apparatus licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `installing or operating it is an offence under s 47` IF
        `the apparatus is broadcasting apparatus` `the apparatus`
    AND (NOT `the operator is exempt by s 20(3)` `the operator`)
    AND (NOT `holds an apparatus licence`)
    AND (NOT `exempted by the Authority`)

§§ `30 -- supporting a proscribed foreign broadcasting service`

-- s 29(4): a "foreign broadcasting service" transmits from outside Singapore services "capable of being received in Singapore"; the
-- Minister may proscribe one by order (s 29(1)).
-- s 30(2): "Any person who in Singapore" does any of (a) supplying equipment or goods for its day-to-day running; (b) supplying or
-- offering to supply programmes; (c) arranging for or inviting others to supply programmes; (d) advertising goods or services on it;
-- (e) publishing programme times or advertising promoting it; (f) supplying or offering to supply decoding equipment designed
-- "primarily" for receiving it; (g) "promoting, financially or otherwise, a proscribed service" commits an offence.
-- (5): "exposing decoding equipment for supply or having such equipment in the person's possession for supply is deemed to offer to
-- supply it". (3): fine up to $40,000 or 3 years or both.
-- Merely watching a proscribed service is not on the list. (A dish to receive it would still need a s 20 licence.)
DECLARE SupportAct IS ONE OF
    `supplying equipment for its day-to-day running`
    `supplying programmes to it`
    `inviting another person to supply programmes`
    `advertising own goods on it`
    `publishing its programme times`
    `displaying its decoders for sale in a shop`
    `paying money to promote it`
    `watching it at home`

GIVEN `the act` IS A SupportAct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is listed in s 30(2)` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `watching it at home` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the act` IS A SupportAct, `done in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the service is proscribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an offence under s 30` IF
    `the act is listed in s 30(2)` `the act` AND `done in Singapore` AND `the service is proscribed`

§§ `48, 48A -- unauthorised decoders`

-- s 48(1): a person must not manufacture, ... sell, ... or otherwise distribute "any decoder which the person knows is an
-- unauthorised decoder". (4): once dealing is proved, "it is presumed, unless there is evidence to the contrary, that the person
-- knew". (2): a person must not "wilfully receive or rebroadcast" an encrypted programme decoded without the lawful provider's
-- authorisation. (3): fine up to $40,000 or 3 years or both; the decoder is forfeited.
-- s 48A(3): a civil action by the lawful provider or copyright owner "must not be brought ... after the expiry of 6 years" from the
-- act. (The exact 6-year boundary is not tested.)
GIVEN `dealt in an unauthorised decoder` IS A BOOLEAN, `there is evidence the dealer did not know` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is an offence under s 48(1)` IF
    `dealt in an unauthorised decoder` AND (NOT `there is evidence the dealer did not know`)

GIVEN `received a programme decoded without authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN, `did so wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reception is an offence under s 48(2)` IF
    `received a programme decoded without authorisation` AND `did so wilfully`

GIVEN `years since the act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a civil action under s 48A may still be brought` IF
    `years since the act` AT MOST 6

§§ `32, 33 -- broadcasting companies and their boards`

-- s 32(2): a "relevant licence" is (a) a free-to-air licence or (b) a subscription broadcasting licence "which permits broadcast
-- which is capable of being received in 50,000 dwelling-houses or more, but does not include any class licence", or (c) any other
-- licence the Minister specifies. A broadcasting company is a company holding one, or its holding company.
-- s 33(1): appointing a chief executive, director or chairperson needs the Authority's approval. (2): "Unless the Authority
-- otherwise approves, the chief executive officer of a broadcasting company and at least one-half of its directors must be citizens
-- of Singapore." (5): fine up to $50,000 and $5,000 a day continuing.
GIVEN `is free-to-air or subscription` IS A BOOLEAN, `dwelling-houses reachable` IS A NUMBER, `is a class licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `specified by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licence is a relevant licence` IF
        `specified by the Minister`
    OR  (`is free-to-air or subscription` AND `dwelling-houses reachable` AT LEAST 50000 AND (NOT `is a class licence`))

GIVEN `the chief executive is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `citizen directors` IS A NUMBER, `all directors` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority approved otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the board meets s 33(2)` IF
        `the Authority approved otherwise`
    OR  (`the chief executive is a citizen` AND `citizen directors` TIMES 2 AT LEAST `all directors`)

§§ `35, 36, 41 -- control of broadcasting companies`

-- s 35(1): a person must not "become a substantial shareholder of a broadcasting company without first obtaining the approval of
-- the Minister". (3): nor enter an agreement to act together over "voting shares of an aggregate of more than 5% of the total votes".
-- s 36(1): nor become "(a) a 12% controller; or (b) an indirect controller". (3): a 12% controller "alone or together with the
-- person's associates" holds "at least 12% of the shares" or controls "voting power of at least 12%".
-- (5): an indirect controller is one whose wishes the directors are accustomed or obliged to follow, or who "is in a position to
-- determine the policy" -- but not (c) an Authority-approved director or officer, nor (d) one whose wishes are followed "by reason
-- only" of professional advice.
-- s 34(1): these sections apply to everyone, "whether resident in Singapore or not and whether citizens of Singapore or not".
GIVEN `directors follow their wishes` IS A BOOLEAN, `can determine policy` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an approved director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `followed only as a professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an indirect controller` IF
        (`directors follow their wishes` OR `can determine policy`)
    AND (NOT `is an approved director or officer`)
    AND (NOT `followed only as a professional adviser`)

GIVEN `would be a substantial shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN, `share percent with associates` IS A NUMBER, `voting percent with associates` IS A NUMBER, `percent of votes under an agreement to act together` IS A NUMBER, `would be an indirect controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Ministerial approval is needed first` IF
        `would be a substantial shareholder`
    OR  `share percent with associates` AT LEAST 12
    OR  `voting percent with associates` AT LEAST 12
    OR  `percent of votes under an agreement to act together` GREATER THAN 5
    OR  `would be an indirect controller`

-- s 41(1): contravening s 35 or s 36(1)(a) (12% controller): fine up to $50,000 and $5,000 a day continuing -- no imprisonment.
-- s 41(2): contravening s 36(1)(b) (indirect controller): fine up to $50,000 "or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years"
-- or both, and $5,000 a day continuing.
DECLARE ControlBreach IS ONE OF
    `becoming a substantial shareholder without approval`
    `becoming a 12% controller without approval`
    `becoming an indirect controller without approval`

GIVEN `the breach` IS A ControlBreach
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `imprisonment is available for the breach` IF
    CONSIDER `the breach`
    WHEN `becoming an indirect controller without approval` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for a control breach` MEANS
    50000 PLUS 5000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 41(3): a defence to a s 35 or s 36 charge to prove (a) the person "was not aware" of the contravention and (b) within 14 days of
-- becoming aware notified the Minister and took the action the Minister directed.
-- (4): for s 36(1) only, even an aware person has a defence if (a) the contravention came from an increase in the holding of a
-- family associate under s 36(4)(c)(i), (b) there is no agreement or arrangement with that associate, and (c) the person notified
-- the Minister "within 14 days of the date of the contravention" and took the directed action.
-- (5): otherwise "it is not a defence ... to prove that the person did not intend to or did not knowingly contravene".
GIVEN `was aware of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to notify the Minister` IS A NUMBER, `took the directed action` IS A BOOLEAN, `charged under s 36(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `caused by a relative's increase` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with that relative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 41 defence is made out` IF
        `took the directed action`
    AND `days to notify the Minister` AT MOST 14
    AND (    (NOT `was aware of the contravention`)
         OR  (`charged under s 36(1)` AND `caused by a relative's increase` AND (NOT `has an arrangement with that relative`)))

§§ `43 -- funds from a foreign source`

-- s 43(9): "foreign source" includes (a) a foreign government or its agent; (b) a company or association constituted under a foreign
-- law; (c) "any person who is not a citizen of Singapore, whether or not he or she is resident in Singapore"; (d) a Singapore body
-- corporate or association "one or more of whose members or directors are not citizens of Singapore" (the deposited text of (d)
-- is garbled; it is read as this); (e) any other source the Minister declares.
-- (1): a person must not, without the Authority's prior consent, receive a fund from a foreign source "for the purposes of
-- financing ... any broadcasting service owned or operated by any broadcasting company". (3): an unsolicited fund must be reported
-- "within 7 days of receiving the fund". (7): "Nothing in this section applies to any dealing ... in the shares of a broadcasting
-- company quoted on a stock exchange in Singapore." (8): fine up to $50,000 or 3 years or both, and forfeiture.
-- (5), (6): an employee who receives a foreign fund to broadcast an item or adopt "a particular line or bias" must report it to the
-- chief executive within 7 days; a fund "received from outside Singapore" is "presumed to be from a foreign source until the
-- contrary is proved".
DECLARE Funder IS ONE OF
    `a foreign government`
    `a company incorporated abroad`
    `a Singapore permanent resident`
    `a Singapore company with one foreign director`
    `a Singapore company owned and run by citizens`
    `a Singapore citizen`

GIVEN `the funder` IS A Funder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the funder is a foreign source` IF
    CONSIDER `the funder`
    WHEN `a Singapore company owned and run by citizens` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the funder` IS A Funder, `to finance a broadcasting company's service` IS A BOOLEAN, `had the Authority's prior consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `a dealing in listed shares` IS A BOOLEAN, `was unsolicited` IS A BOOLEAN, `days taken to report it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `receiving the fund is an offence under s 43` IF
        `the funder is a foreign source` `the funder`
    AND `to finance a broadcasting company's service`
    AND (NOT `had the Authority's prior consent`)
    AND (NOT `a dealing in listed shares`)
    AND ((NOT `was unsolicited`) OR `days taken to report it` GREATER THAN 7)

GIVEN `received from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved not a foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN, `to broadcast an item or adopt a line` IS A BOOLEAN, `days to report to the chief executive` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee commits an offence under s 43(5)` IF
        `received from outside Singapore`
    AND (NOT `proved not a foreign source`)
    AND `to broadcast an item or adopt a line`
    AND `days to report to the chief executive` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `44 -- broadcasting company owned by a foreign source`

-- s 44(1): "unless the Minister otherwise approves", a company must not be granted or hold a relevant licence if foreign sources
-- together (a) hold "at least 49% of the shares" or control "voting power of at least 49%" in it or its holding company, or (b) "all
-- or a majority" of those managing it are appointed by, or act on the wishes of, foreign sources. (2): without approval the Authority
-- "must" cancel the licence "without any compensation".
GIVEN `foreign share percent` IS A NUMBER, `foreign voting percent` IS A NUMBER, `management mostly foreign-directed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister approves` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the company may hold a relevant licence` IF
        `the Minister approves`
    OR  (    `foreign share percent` LESS THAN 49
         AND `foreign voting percent` LESS THAN 49
         AND (NOT `management mostly foreign-directed`))

§§ `45D -- egregious content`

-- s 45D(1): "egregious content" is content that (a) advocates or instructs on suicide or self-harm; (b) on violence, torture or
-- serious physical harm to human beings; (c) on sexual violence or coercion; (d) depicts for a sexual purpose or exploits the nudity
-- of a child; (e) advocates conduct obstructing a public health measure or creating a public health risk in Singapore; (f) deals
-- with race or religion in a way likely to cause enmity, hatred, ill will or hostility against different racial or religious groups
-- in Singapore; (g) advocates or instructs on terrorism; or (h) is prescribed by Part 10A regulations (none read: treated as empty).
-- (2): "It does not matter if the content ... relates to conduct engaged in within or outside Singapore."
DECLARE Content IS ONE OF
    `a post encouraging self-harm`
    `a video instructing on torture`
    `a post advocating sexual coercion`
    `sexualised images of a child`
    `a post urging people to defy a quarantine order`
    `a post stirring hatred between religious groups`
    `a video instructing on bomb-making for terrorism`
    `a post criticising a government policy`
    `a defamatory post about a private person`
    `a holiday video`

GIVEN `the content` IS A Content
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the content is egregious` IF
    CONSIDER `the content`
    WHEN `a post criticising a government policy` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a defamatory post about a private person` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a holiday video` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `45E, 45G, 45H, 45J -- online communication services`

-- s 45H(1): the Authority may direct a provider whose service has a Singapore end-user link to disable access to egregious content.
-- (3): a requirement "must not relate to any user-generated content that is communication between 2 or more end-users that is of a
-- private or domestic nature".
-- s 45E(1): an offence if the provider (a) provides the service with a Singapore end-user link, (c) the content is egregious, (d)
-- knows or ought reasonably to know, and (e) fails in its s 45J duty -- "to take all reasonably practicable steps to comply" -- with
-- a s 45H direction. (3): "immaterial" whether provided from outside Singapore. (4): if the content was accessible when the direction
-- was given, knowledge "must be presumed until the contrary is proved".
-- s 45G: a defence to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that "it was not reasonably practicable to do more than what was in fact
-- done" and "there was no better practicable means".
-- s 45E(2): fine up to $1 million and up to $100,000 a day continuing after conviction. No imprisonment.
GIVEN `the content` IS A Content, `accessible by Singapore end-users` IS A BOOLEAN, `private or domestic communication between end-users` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 45H direction may cover the content` IF
        `the content is egregious` `the content`
    AND `accessible by Singapore end-users`
    AND (NOT `private or domestic communication between end-users`)

GIVEN `the content` IS A Content, `service has a Singapore end-user link` IS A BOOLEAN, `accessible when the direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `provider proved it did not know` IS A BOOLEAN, `failed to comply with the direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `provider proved the s 45G defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provider commits an offence under s 45E` IF
        `service has a Singapore end-user link`
    AND `the content is egregious` `the content`
    AND `accessible when the direction was given`
    AND (NOT `provider proved it did not know`)
    AND `failed to comply with the direction`
    AND (NOT `provider proved the s 45G defence`)

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 45E` MEANS
    1000000 PLUS 100000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

§§ `45F, 45I -- internet access services`

-- s 45I(2): if a provider "fails to comply" with a s 45H direction, the Authority may direct an internet access service provider "to
-- stop access by Singapore end-users to the online communication service" -- the whole service, not just the content.
-- s 45F(1): an offence for the internet access provider who fails in its s 45J duty to comply with that blocking direction (with the
-- same knowledge elements and presumption, and the s 45G defence).
-- s 45F(2): fine "not exceeding $20,000 for each day or part of a day" of non-compliance "but not exceeding a total fine of
-- $500,000".
GIVEN `the platform failed a s 45H direction` IS A BOOLEAN, `the access provider controls access` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 45I blocking direction may be given` IF
    `the platform failed a s 45H direction` AND `the access provider controls access`

GIVEN `days of non-compliance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine under s 45F` MEANS
    `the smaller of` (20000 TIMES `days of non-compliance`) 500000
